#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:5
#: c573b98d749943feaeea4096b8dc7b1b
msgid "Hargrave Technologies DroneCAN ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:9
#: 851884a50cc740db892e0a8a53a6833a
msgid "Hargrave Technologies is an Australian power electronics engineering company specialising in the professional design and manufacturing of NDAA-compliant electronic speed controllers (ESCs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:11
#: b907905e027e4a9fb9674928d581ae67
msgid "Hargrave's ESCs are designed for space and weight-limited applications and optimised for power density while maintaining optimum thermal performance. `The full range can be found here <https://www.hargravetechnologies.com/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:13
#: 10084e631dd0444dbdd6b55f2bfcce33
msgid "The ESCs support DroneCAN natively, providing an interface for control, telemetry, parameter configuration and firmware updates. The following guide describes how to get set up and outlines the main features of the DroneCAN interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:17
#: 083e161ac97242f1823729b65217e8d4
msgid "Ardupilot Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:18
#: 257f7a4e79f54ed587284affa76ff6f2
msgid "Follow the instructions for DroneCAN setup found at :ref:`DroneCAN ESCs <common-uavcan-escs>` - specifically, the parameters required for the autopilot to activate the DroneCAN driver on the desired physical port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:22
#: 5e06b74a64b04fe28c8939732b4b9799
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:23
#: 25b8d4358d054655b2a038b36661e129
msgid "By default, the ESCs will accept a CAN Bus communications input. The ESCs can be configured over USB or CAN Bus. `A USB configuration tool for settings, onboard log view and firmware updates can be found here <https://configurator.hargravetechnologies.com>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:27
#: 2d092f305cc546eda6c9809c94c5b7dc
msgid "To enable CAN, the `CAN Bus Enabled <https://docs.hargravetechnologies.com/communication-settings>`__ setting should be set as required. The settings names are abbreviated for CAN transmissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:29
#: 316c151992eb460bbd97bd0228ba9c2b
msgid "When running DroneCAN, it's recommended to set the DroneCAN Node ID as required by the system, noting there should be no duplicates. By default, Hargrave ESCs will seek a Node ID automatically (the flight controller will negotiate and provide one through dynamic node allocation). However, this can result in changing IDs over time. The following ESC settings will change this behaviour:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:31
#: 51729129b3a44d7fa5ff386d61f3cf66
msgid "``Force DroneCAN Node ID (FORCE_NODEID)``:  Toggles the method that the ESC uses to get an ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:32
#: 044a639249c747068fc7b3455d574b74
msgid "``Preferred DroneCAN Node ID (DRONECAN_NODEID)``:  Set the desired Node ID. The ESC will use this ID when the Force Node ID parameter is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:34
#: 762a1550d1b24ec99233256fe7481300
msgid "Further settings that should be considered (more documentation can be found `here <https://docs.hargravetechnologies.com/can-bus-settings>`__):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:36
#: 5ebddcf1d7a74918889476f126337d73
msgid "``DroneCAN ESC Index (DRONECAN_INDEX)``:  Configures which motor output the ESC will use from the flight controller. The channels are 0 indexed, so Motor 1 on the flight controller is ``ESC Index`` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:37
#: f6529d1c3f634330832b00607b157879
msgid "``Require Armed Status DroneCAN (CAN_ARM_CHK_EN)``:  By default, the ESC will only drive the motor while the Autopilot broadcasts that it is in an Armed state. Toggle this setting to change the behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:38
#: 5daf29e297f448159890e260185083f7
msgid "``CAN Terminator Enable (CAN_TERM_EN)``:  The onboard software-selectable CAN termination resistor can be enabled by toggling this setting. Follow the connection tips below to select which ESC to enable this on, as it should only be enabled on a single unit per bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:41
#: 1f33f824e0d547349ccddbb0f4857534
msgid "Connecting the ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:42
#: 4505f5d34c9f42f5a668256b18cc1e33
msgid "Each ESC should be connected in a daisy chain configuration, where one end of the chain is the flight controller, and the other is an ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:46
#: b5a6bd2792754d838ca8a60029bdb4a3
msgid "Ensure the flight controller is appropriately terminated. For example, models such as the Pixhawk Cube have CAN termination resistors installed by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:48
#: c1b40e1b05284b50a76be82cd315168e
msgid "The CAN H, CAN L and GND should be connected to the flight controller ports in the same order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:52
#: fc900530ed7c411a99814aea76099854
msgid "The ESCs have a software-selectable CAN termination resistor for ease of integration, which should be enabled on the ESC that is physically furthest along the daisy chain (in reference to the flight controller)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:54
#: 972e4ab1b66242e2a9d7f9c16519b6d6
msgid "The following diagram shows the wiring of the CAN lines communicating from the flight controller, and terminating on the final ESC (which should have the terminator activated):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:59
#: e8d69df47a86419ba650e2b6fee7a67b
msgid "Logging and Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:61
#: d633325af7074d87a9fa6114f61f795c
msgid "The ESCs support telemetry reporting directly to the autopilot, for viewing and logging purposes. Ardupilot log viewing tools can be used to view this data. The ESCs support two different telemetry messages which can be individually configured as required, transmitting the following data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:64
#: 78901c9521d0416e9ea4d397561fac83
msgid "ESC Primary Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:65
#: c759ea3d4cf445849fc0cb1f2facdf76
msgid "Error Count:  Current active errors on the ESC. 0 indicates no errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:66
#: 35fa3330914d4906b8e1df8500b58893
msgid "Voltage:  The bus voltage currently measured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:67
#: d0c4cef80c93430c9d1a218bba087ec7
msgid "Current:  The bus current currently measured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:68
#: ed068895919542f9beb09d28144cce24
msgid "Temperature:  The bridge temperature currently measured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:69
#: cf509693dcb24c3f9243d28275a01543
msgid "RPM:  The RPM of the motor, scaled with the ``Motor Pole Pair`` parameter on the ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:70
#: 1cf20ea279ef4dd7b010e349ad63cb7d
msgid "Requested Power:  The percentage power currently requested by the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:74
#: 4714d9ea41dd44618b586bb8dfc1ebd0
msgid "ESC Extended Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:75
#: 2f00af3071cd45bf8495e6f48ee483e7
msgid "Input Percent:  The percentage duty cycle currently requested by the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:76
#: c0d0fad2e92046cca5bbd6534035571b
msgid "Output Percent:  The percentage duty cycle currently output to the motor. If not equal to input percent, this indicates limiting is occurring within the ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:77
#: a09886546210419f821325b33b377a96
msgid "Motor Temperature:  The temperature of the connected motor (requires NTC or PTC sensor connected to the ESC)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:78
#: 981ed6f902144da7b7851fa1cfb6bbbc
msgid "Motor Angle:  The currently measured angle of the motor, if sensor input is enabled. (requires external motor position sensing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:79
#: cf20ea939b8f49fe965a1259b261b20f
msgid "Status Flags:  The current general status of the ESC, non-error specific."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:82
#: bf906a0fbbf849beaf6ce560427aa5ca
msgid "Both status messages are individually transmitted, and the rate can be adjusted separately as required. The rate of transmission should be minimised such that the CAN bus is not overloaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:85
#: 33302e818d564a919d75dc79ec3b4c4f
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:87
#: 91300da574c241a49030bc2124628ac2
msgid "The ESCs support parameter/setting configuration over DroneCAN. The ESC will reboot to apply the updates to the parameters. By default, not all settings are shown. To show all available parameters on the ESC, enable the ``Advanced Settings`` parameter (the ESC will require a reboot to apply and allow fetching of all parameters). Once set, this setting will persist until changed again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:91
#: 4b7984957d044c0cb288bd69d1f78e8f
msgid "If CAN is disabled, USB access is required to configure the ESC from serial signalling mode back into CAN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:93
#: a733d32dd3974c1885dd780381675231
msgid "The ESC will reject attempts to fetch or save parameters while the motor is running (or the ESC is in the motor driving state). To perform further updates, either disarm the motors (assuming the ``Require Armed Status DroneCAN`` parameter is enabled) or disable the ESC throttle packet output from the flight controller. Rebooting the ESC will also allow for parameter changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:95
#: 05ceb4fe817b4c04802a09235a57b920
msgid "The ``Erase All`` function within DroneCAN will reset the configuration to the default state, and automatically trigger a reboot to apply the settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:98
#: 7d9689dc5227437691bd594aa80fb23e
msgid "Firmware Updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:100
#: c0007a1b960e493db3181644055b5fa2
msgid "The ESCs support firmware updating over DroneCAN. Once the firmware update process has started, the ESC will report file read and update status through the DroneCAN debug messages. The ESCs automatically check the file for compatibility before the update starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:102
#: 9ffcf05044454dc8ba5f86136b19040c
msgid "Once the firmware is successfully downloaded, the unit will automatically verify and perform the firmware installation, followed by a reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:106
#: 38bef87d9ef94927a6d530fab6aa169f
msgid "The ESCs have a built in recovery in the event the update process is interrupted or fails to complete. If an issue occurs, reboot the unit and restart the update attempt. The previous firmware version is retained in the event of interruption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:108
#: e090bdda1b1249389b2bac49551e182f
msgid "The firmware can be updated through the DroneCAN GUI or other DroneCAN-supported interfaces (such as Mission Planner). The image below highlights some key DroneCAN GUI features; double-click on a node to open the node properties panel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:112
#: 4d0d29c253614d25b0f5af010cdb3004
msgid "After a firmware update is complete and the unit reboots, confirm the reported firmware version matches expectations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:115
#: aee374fdc49843a5a3f00773df36e90f
msgid "Further Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hargrave-dronecan-escs.rst:117
#: 1bec41c4136b4e2a8dc3702ef974d1a4
msgid "Hargrave Technologies prides itself on industry-leading support. If you have further questions or need assistance, reach out to the team `here <https://www.hargravetechnologies.com/contact>`__. All support topics are channelled directly to the engineering team."
msgstr ""
